{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "BSB",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 109,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.109.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the choirmaster. A Psalm of David. O God of my praise, be not silent.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.109.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For wicked and deceitful mouths open against me; they speak against me with lying tongues.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.109.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They surround me with hateful words and attack me without cause.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.109.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In return for my love they accuse me, but I am a man of prayer.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.109.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They repay me evil for good, and hatred for my love.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.109.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Set over him a wicked man; let an accuser stand at his right hand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.109.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When he is tried, let him be found guilty, and may his prayer be regarded as sin.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.109.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "May his days be few; may another take his position.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.109.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "May his children be fatherless and his wife a widow.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.109.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "May his children wander as beggars, seeking sustenance far from their ruined homes.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.109.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "May the creditor seize all he owns, and strangers plunder the fruits of his labor.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.109.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "May there be no one to extend kindness to him, and no one to favor his fatherless children.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.109.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "May his descendants be cut off; may their name be blotted out from the next generation.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.109.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "May the iniquity of his fathers be remembered before the LORD, and the sin of his mother never be blotted out.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.109.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "May their sins always remain before the LORD, that He may cut off their memory from the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.109.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he never thought to show kindness, but pursued the poor and needy and brokenhearted, even to their death.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.109.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The cursing that he loved, may it fall on him; the blessing in which he refused to delight, may it be far from him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.109.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The cursing that he wore like a coat, may it soak into his body like water, and into his bones like oil.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.109.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "May it be like a robe wrapped about him, like a belt tied forever around him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.109.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "May this be the LORD’s reward to my accusers, to those who speak evil against me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.109.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But You, O GOD, the Lord, deal kindly with me for the sake of Your name; deliver me by the goodness of Your loving devotion.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.109.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I am poor and needy; my heart is wounded within me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.109.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I am fading away like a lengthening shadow; I am shaken off like a locust.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.109.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My knees are weak from fasting, and my body grows lean and gaunt.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.109.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I am an object of scorn to my accusers; when they see me, they shake their heads.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.109.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Help me, O LORD my God; save me according to Your loving devotion.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.109.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let them know that this is Your hand, that You, O LORD, have done it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.109.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Though they curse, You will bless. When they rise up, they will be put to shame, but Your servant will rejoice.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.109.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "May my accusers be clothed with disgrace; may they wear their shame like a robe.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.109.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "With my mouth I will thank the LORD profusely; I will praise Him in the presence of many.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.109.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For He stands at the right hand of the needy one, to save him from the condemners of his soul.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
